# Two qualifying tracks: read_sweep returns the FIRST one met by
# graph.subjects(martigliPeriodInitial, None).  rdflib's Memory store yields
# those subjects grouped by object value, in the order each value was first
# seen: here 9.5 (ex:incomplete), then 8.0 (ex:flat, ex:sweepB, in no
# promised order between them), then 7.0 (ex:sweepA) - so ex:sweepB is
# returned although ex:sweepA is written first.
@prefix sstim: <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

# Met first, alone under its value, and incomplete: the missing-value guard
# must skip it (without the guard, float(None) raises).
ex:incomplete
    sstim:martigliPeriodInitial 9.5 ;
    sstim:martigliPeriodFinal 9.0 .

# Shares its initial period with ex:sweepB, but flat: skipped whichever of
# the two the store yields first.
ex:flat
    sstim:martigliPeriodInitial 8.0 ;
    sstim:martigliPeriodFinal 8.0 ;
    sstim:martigliTransitionDuration 5.0 .

ex:sweepA
    sstim:martigliPeriodInitial 7.0 ;
    sstim:martigliPeriodFinal 1.0 ;
    sstim:martigliTransitionDuration 10.0 .

ex:sweepB
    sstim:martigliPeriodInitial 8.0 ;
    sstim:martigliPeriodFinal 2.0 ;
    sstim:martigliTransitionDuration 20.0 .
